      <!-- ═══ AUTOMATION · GUARDRAILS ═══ -->
      <section class="view" data-view="guardrails" hidden>
      <div class="vtab-row" role="tablist" aria-label="Routing Rules">
        <button class="vtab" data-go="routing" role="tab">Routing</button>
        <button class="vtab" data-go="guardrails" role="tab">Rules</button>
      </div>

        <div class="ph"><div class="ph-l"><h2>Rules</h2><div class="ph-d">The safety net — never post spam, never flood, never double-post. Dedupe and post-shaping switches live in Settings · General, where they shape every post.</div></div></div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-h">AI safety screen <%- icon('shield','icon') %></div>
          <div class="card-b"><div class="sw-grid" id="swRules"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-h">Rules <%- icon('shield','icon') %></div>
          <div class="card-b">
            <p class="muted tiny f-help">Always on (not switches). Blocklist: posts containing any of these words are never published. Rate guard: max posts per hour to protect your channel from floods.</p>
            <div class="field" style="margin-top:12px"><label>Blocklist</label><textarea class="in" id="setBlocklist" rows="2" placeholder="blocked, words, comma separated (empty = off)"></textarea></div>
            <label class="tgl-row" style="margin-top:10px"><input type="checkbox" id="setBlocklistRegex"><span>Interpret blocklist entries as <b>patterns</b> <span class="muted tiny">(off = plain words. Pattern mode: one pattern per line — patterns may contain commas. An invalid pattern is skipped, never fatal)</span></span></label>
            <div class="field" style="margin-top:12px"><label>Find → replace <span class="muted tiny">— one rule per line, old text=>new text, leave new empty to delete</span></label><textarea class="in" id="setReplace" rows="3" placeholder="Join our channel=>&#10;Old Brand=>New Brand&#10;typo=>correction"></textarea></div>
            <div id="replaceRulesBox" style="margin-top:10px"></div>
            <div class="row-form wrap" style="margin-top:12px">
              <input class="in" id="setMaxPerHour" type="number" min="3" placeholder="Max posts per hour (default 30)" style="flex:none;width:auto">
              <button class="btn btn-p" id="guardSave" style="flex:none">Save guardrails</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-h">Per-target rate caps <%- icon('gauge','icon') %></div>
          <div class="card-b">
            <p class="muted tiny f-help">A stricter hourly cap per target channel. <b>0 = follow the global guard</b> above. The cap skips only that target — other targets still get the post, and nothing is ever dropped.</p>
            <div class="tw" style="margin-top:12px"><table class="t" id="grTargetsTable"><thead><tr><th>Target</th><th class="num">Last hour</th><th>Max posts / hour</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
            <div class="row-actions" style="margin-top:10px"><button class="btn btn-p" id="grSave">Save rate caps</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- 5J (J8): pacing visualizer — where today's posts landed vs the cap -->
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-h">Pacing <%- icon('gauge','icon') %> <span class="muted tiny" id="paceNow"></span></div>
          <div class="card-b">
            <p class="muted tiny f-help">The last 24 hours, Pakistan time — one bar per hour with the posts published in it. The dashed line is the rate-guard cap; if any hour reaches it, the pipeline holds back (an honest “rate guard” skip) until the next hour. No automation — this only shows what happened.</p>
            <div class="pace-chart" id="paceChart"></div>
            <div class="muted tiny" id="paceFoot" style="margin-top:8px"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-h">Freshness guard <span class="muted tiny">5I · OFF by default</span></div>
          <div class="card-b">
            <p class="muted tiny f-help">Skip posts older than the age below — for example, a channel you follow that only posts once a month. <b>0 = OFF</b> (today's behaviour: every fresh pipeline event is considered, dedupe still applies). The check runs before the media fetch, with an honest "stale" skip reason.</p>
            <div class="row-form wrap" style="margin-top:12px">
              <input class="in" id="freshHours" type="number" min="0" max="720" placeholder="Max post age in hours (0 = off)" style="flex:none;width:auto" title="Posts older than this are skipped — 0 turns the guard off">
              <button class="btn btn-p" id="freshSave" style="flex:none">Save freshness</button>
              <span class="muted tiny" id="freshState"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══ INBOX · WHATSAPP (official WhatsApp-Web look — permanent) ═══ -->
